1
00:00:01,921 --> 00:00:03,298
Hoo, hoo!

2
00:00:03,410 --> 00:00:04,337
Hi!

3
00:00:04,387 --> 00:00:06,414
It's me, Popcorn!

4
00:00:06,536 --> 00:00:11,767
Welcome to Popcorn Tales, the
cozy nest of bedtime stories.

5
00:00:12,079 --> 00:00:15,502
Hug your teddy, because
tonight's story is:

6
00:00:15,552 --> 00:00:18,426
The Frog Prince and the Golden Ball!

7
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:26,860
Once upon a time, when wishing
still made a difference,

8
00:00:26,910 --> 00:00:31,860
there lived a king who had several
daughters, and the youngest was so lovely

9
00:00:31,910 --> 00:00:34,658
that even the sun stopped to look at her.

10
00:00:35,321 --> 00:00:38,799
The youngest princess's
favorite toy was a golden ball,

11
00:00:38,849 --> 00:00:41,694
which shone like a
little piece of the sun.

12
00:00:42,344 --> 00:00:47,308
On warm afternoons, she went into the
forest near the castle and sat at the

13
00:00:47,358 --> 00:00:52,133
edge of a deep well, in the
shade of a huge old tree.

14
00:00:55,682 --> 00:00:59,596
There she threw the golden ball up
into the air and caught it again,

15
00:00:59,710 --> 00:01:03,957
laughing and laughing, because it
was the game she loved most of all.

16
00:01:04,515 --> 00:01:05,892
Hoo, hoo!

17
00:01:05,995 --> 00:01:07,684
What a shiny ball!

18
00:01:07,789 --> 00:01:10,432
I just hope it doesn't fall anywhere,

19
00:01:10,482 --> 00:01:12,923
Popcorn said, from the branch.

20
00:01:14,039 --> 00:01:18,105
But one day, the princess
threw the ball much too high,

21
00:01:18,233 --> 00:01:22,314
it slipped through her hands,
and it fell right into the well.

22
00:01:24,474 --> 00:01:27,999
The water was so deep that
nobody could see the bottom,

23
00:01:28,085 --> 00:01:32,151
and the princess began to
cry, louder and louder.

24
00:01:32,723 --> 00:01:34,838
What's the matter, princess?

25
00:01:34,913 --> 00:01:38,465
You're crying so sadly that even
the stones feel sorry for you,

26
00:01:38,515 --> 00:01:42,429
said the croaky voice of a
frog, close to the water.

27
00:01:43,067 --> 00:01:47,531
The princess looked around and
saw a green frog with golden eyes,

28
00:01:47,581 --> 00:01:49,620
poking his head out of the water.

29
00:01:50,198 --> 00:01:54,425
Oh, frog, my golden ball fell into the
well, and I will never be able to get

30
00:01:54,475 --> 00:01:55,278
it back,

31
00:01:55,328 --> 00:01:59,145
the princess answered,
wiping away her tears.

32
00:01:59,667 --> 00:02:03,837
I can fetch your ball, princess,
but what will you give me in return?

33
00:02:03,887 --> 00:02:07,370
the frog asked, paddling
his feet in the water.

34
00:02:08,385 --> 00:02:09,903
I'll give you anything you like:

35
00:02:09,953 --> 00:02:13,050
my dresses, my pearls,
even my golden crown!

36
00:02:13,100 --> 00:02:14,972
the princess said quickly.

37
00:02:15,536 --> 00:02:18,609
I don't want dresses or jewels, princess.

38
00:02:18,719 --> 00:02:20,238
I only want to be your friend:

39
00:02:20,288 --> 00:02:24,516
to eat from your plate, drink from your
cup, and sleep near you in the castle,

40
00:02:24,566 --> 00:02:27,410
the frog said, with shining eyes.

41
00:02:28,051 --> 00:02:29,537
The princess thought:

42
00:02:29,587 --> 00:02:32,525
What nonsense, a frog
can't live in a castle!

43
00:02:32,575 --> 00:02:35,948
But out loud, she promised him all of it.

44
00:02:36,589 --> 00:02:41,387
The frog dived down very deep, and soon
came back with the golden ball in his

45
00:02:41,437 --> 00:02:44,406
mouth, and tossed it onto the grass.

46
00:02:46,584 --> 00:02:50,173
The princess picked up the
ball, gave a shout of joy,

47
00:02:50,223 --> 00:02:53,984
and ran off to the castle
without even looking back.

48
00:02:54,551 --> 00:02:57,171
Wait, princess, wait for me!

49
00:02:57,280 --> 00:02:59,320
I can't run as fast as that,

50
00:02:59,370 --> 00:03:01,812
the frog called out, hopping after her.

51
00:03:02,883 --> 00:03:07,472
The next evening, the king, the
princess and the whole court were having

52
00:03:07,522 --> 00:03:12,055
dinner, when someone came up
the marble stairs very slowly,

53
00:03:12,105 --> 00:03:14,658
with a wet, squishy sound.

54
00:03:17,542 --> 00:03:21,937
Then there was a knock at the door,
and the frog's croaky voice called out:

55
00:03:21,987 --> 00:03:25,645
Princess, youngest princess,
open the door for me!

56
00:03:27,356 --> 00:03:32,431
The princess opened the door, saw
the frog, slammed it shut again,

57
00:03:32,481 --> 00:03:35,422
and went back to the
table looking frightened.

58
00:03:35,997 --> 00:03:38,758
My daughter, why do you look like that?

59
00:03:38,818 --> 00:03:40,611
Is there a giant out there?

60
00:03:40,661 --> 00:03:42,991
the king asked, worried.

61
00:03:43,597 --> 00:03:47,946
It isn't a giant, Father, it's a frog,
who fetched my ball from the well,

62
00:03:47,996 --> 00:03:50,119
and I promised that he could be my friend,

63
00:03:50,169 --> 00:03:52,833
the princess answered, looking down.

64
00:03:53,423 --> 00:03:58,351
A promise is a serious thing, my daughter,
and what you promise must be done.

65
00:03:58,591 --> 00:04:00,408
Go and let the frog come in,

66
00:04:00,458 --> 00:04:02,927
the king said, in a firm voice.

67
00:04:04,026 --> 00:04:08,921
The princess opened the door, and the
frog hopped in and followed her all the

68
00:04:08,971 --> 00:04:10,315
way to her chair.

69
00:04:13,147 --> 00:04:17,265
Please lift me up onto the table,
princess, so I can eat beside you,

70
00:04:17,315 --> 00:04:18,743
the frog asked.

71
00:04:19,387 --> 00:04:24,323
At first, the princess felt a little
disgusted, but then she noticed that the

72
00:04:24,373 --> 00:04:28,731
frog ate very politely,
and even used a napkin.

73
00:04:29,379 --> 00:04:34,649
The frog told stories about the forest,
about the stars reflected in the well,

74
00:04:34,699 --> 00:04:39,677
and about the firefly parties along the
riverbank, and the princess began to

75
00:04:39,727 --> 00:04:40,927
laugh.

76
00:04:41,303 --> 00:04:43,418
You are very funny, frog!

77
00:04:43,557 --> 00:04:46,132
I never knew a frog could
know so many things,

78
00:04:46,182 --> 00:04:49,152
the princess said, feeling calmer now.

79
00:04:49,740 --> 00:04:51,117
Hoo, hoo!

80
00:04:51,225 --> 00:04:56,587
Look at that, the princess is finding
out that the frog is a wonderful friend,

81
00:04:56,637 --> 00:04:59,773
Popcorn said, winking at the king.

82
00:05:00,858 --> 00:05:05,822
When it grew late, the frog yawned
and said he was very sleepy,

83
00:05:05,872 --> 00:05:08,578
and asked to sleep in the princess's room.

84
00:05:09,235 --> 00:05:13,101
The princess thought for a moment
and remembered her promise,

85
00:05:13,151 --> 00:05:16,024
and this time she did not complain.

86
00:05:16,669 --> 00:05:21,916
She took a soft red velvet cushion,
placed it on the floor beside her bed,

87
00:05:21,975 --> 00:05:25,069
and covered the frog
with a silk handkerchief.

88
00:05:25,682 --> 00:05:27,884
Good night, my friend the frog.

89
00:05:28,006 --> 00:05:32,153
I'm sorry I ran away from you in the
forest, I should never have done that,

90
00:05:32,203 --> 00:05:34,270
the princess said, kindly.

91
00:05:34,854 --> 00:05:36,726
Good night, princess.

92
00:05:36,776 --> 00:05:39,681
Thank you for keeping your
promise with all your heart,

93
00:05:39,731 --> 00:05:43,173
the frog answered,
closing his golden eyes.

94
00:05:43,325 --> 00:05:47,892
The next morning, when the first ray
of sunshine came through the window,

95
00:05:47,978 --> 00:05:49,975
something wonderful happened.

96
00:05:53,555 --> 00:05:58,352
Where the frog had been, there stood a
young prince with brown hair and golden

97
00:05:58,402 --> 00:06:01,260
eyes, just like the frog's eyes.

98
00:06:01,901 --> 00:06:03,876
Don't be afraid, princess.

99
00:06:04,059 --> 00:06:08,796
A sorceress turned me into a frog a
long time ago, and only a princess who

100
00:06:08,846 --> 00:06:12,037
kept her promise with all her
heart could break the spell,

101
00:06:12,087 --> 00:06:14,376
the prince said, smiling.

102
00:06:15,031 --> 00:06:18,759
The princess was so happy
that she laughed with joy,

103
00:06:18,809 --> 00:06:22,390
and the two of them ran off
to tell the king everything.

104
00:06:23,504 --> 00:06:28,098
Soon after, a white and golden
carriage arrived at the castle,

105
00:06:28,156 --> 00:06:31,904
pulled by eight white horses
with plumes on their heads.

106
00:06:36,914 --> 00:06:41,467
At the front of the carriage rode
faithful Henry, the prince's servant,

107
00:06:41,567 --> 00:06:45,850
who had been so sad about the spell
that he had put three iron bands around

108
00:06:45,900 --> 00:06:49,911
his chest, to keep his heart
from breaking with sorrow.

109
00:06:50,554 --> 00:06:55,490
When he saw the prince again, Henry's
heart was so happy that the three iron

110
00:06:55,540 --> 00:06:58,940
bands snapped open, one after another.

111
00:07:00,670 --> 00:07:02,308
Henry, what was that noise?

112
00:07:02,500 --> 00:07:03,727
Is the carriage breaking?

113
00:07:03,777 --> 00:07:05,968
the prince asked, worried.

114
00:07:06,530 --> 00:07:10,347
No, my prince, those are the
iron bands around my heart,

115
00:07:10,397 --> 00:07:12,612
coming loose because I am so happy,

116
00:07:12,662 --> 00:07:15,048
Henry answered, smiling.

117
00:07:15,689 --> 00:07:19,153
The prince and the princess
became the best of friends,

118
00:07:19,203 --> 00:07:23,708
and later they were married, and every
year they held a party at the edge of

119
00:07:23,758 --> 00:07:25,297
the forest well.

120
00:07:25,878 --> 00:07:27,255
Hoo, hoo!

121
00:07:27,369 --> 00:07:32,384
A promise is a serious thing, and when
we are kind to those who are different,

122
00:07:32,434 --> 00:07:34,197
we make true friends,

123
00:07:34,247 --> 00:07:37,620
Popcorn said, blinking her big eyes.

124
00:07:44,924 --> 00:07:46,124
The End.

125
00:07:47,839 --> 00:07:48,551
Hoo...

126
00:07:48,601 --> 00:07:49,626
Psst!

127
00:07:49,676 --> 00:07:51,247
Are you still awake?

128
00:07:51,400 --> 00:07:53,454
Did you like tonight's story?

129
00:07:53,564 --> 00:07:57,342
The princess showed us that
a promise is a serious thing,

130
00:07:57,392 --> 00:08:01,574
and that when we are kind to others,
even those who look different,

131
00:08:01,624 --> 00:08:03,482
we make true friends.

132
00:08:03,768 --> 00:08:08,075
Good night, sleep tight, and
have the sweetest dreams.

133
00:08:08,371 --> 00:08:13,269
Grown-ups: if you enjoyed it,
please subscribe to Popcorn Tales,

134
00:08:13,319 --> 00:08:15,724
for more stories at bedtime.

135
00:08:16,028 --> 00:08:17,228
Hoo...

